			"notes": "# Changelog\n## Bug fixes\n- Peeled walnut does not have a recipe.\n- All the mod furnaces have the same cooking time.\n## Gameplay changes\n- Now, Mate has 10 uses per charge, and when its durability reaches 0, it gives the player an Empty mate. It works simillar to potions and honey bottles.\n\t- Also, his recipe has been changed. Is no longer required that the Grounded yerba mate is up of the Empty mate.\n- Added new Frostbite effect: it gives the player the same effect that when they enter Powder snow, including the slowness, the frozen hearts GUI and the freezing screen. Leveling this effect only amplies his duration.\n- Added new Frostbite enchantment: it can be aplied to daggers, swords and axes. Applies Frostbite to the target, and his max level is II.\n\t- If your weapon has Frosbite, it can't have Fire aspect, Living touch and/or Poison touch, and viseversa.\n## Blocks\n- Added Cold lyrium: a new flower that is generated on snowy biomes. Is used to get Vegetable fibber on early game, and it can also be used on Light gray dye production.\n- Added Succulent: a new flower that is generated on desert biomes. Is used to get Vegetable fibber on early game, and it can also be used on Lime dye production.\n## World generation\n- Ore generation of almost all the modded ores has been reworked. Here is the list of changes:\n- Tin ore now tries to generate 3 separate times, with the following order:\n\t- Between y=-40 and y=30, the game will try to generate a max of 7 Tin betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 20% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t- Between y=20 and y=120, the game will try to generate a max of 12 Tin betas per chunk, with a max size of 12 ores per beta.\n\t- Between y=90 and y=140, the game will try to generate a max of 6 Tin betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 20% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\n\n- Zinc ore, on the overworld, now tries to generate 2 separate times, with the following order:\n\t- Between y=-80 and y=-10, the game will try to generate a max of 9 Zinc betas per chunk, with a max size of 10 ores per beta. It has a 30% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t- Between y=-10 and y=30, the game will try to generate a max of 6 Zinc betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 20% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\n\n- Sulfur ore, on the overworld, now tries to generate 3 separate times, with the following order:\n\t- Between y=-90 and y=20, the game will try to generate a max of 8 Sulfur betas per chunk, with a max size of 9 ores per beta. It has a 40% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t- Between y=-10 and y=160, the game will try to generate a max of 6 Sulfur betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 20% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t- Between y=70 and y=190, the game will try to generate a max of 5 Sulfur betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 20% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\n\n- Silver ore now tries to generate 3 separate times, with the following order:\n\t- Between y=-64 and y=32, the game will try to generate a max of 6 Silver betas per chunk, with a max size of 5 ores per beta. It has a 50% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t- Between y=-40 and y=20, the game will try to generate a max of 4 Silver betas per chunk, with a max size of 5 ores per beta. It has a 50% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\t-On badlands biomes, between y=-64 and y=260, the game will try to generate a max of 10 Silver betas per chunk, with a max size of 5 ores per beta.\n\n- Sapphire ore now tries to generate 2 separate times, with the following order:\n\t- On Jungle and Lush caves biomes, between y=-70 and y=-40, the game will try to generate a max of 8 Sapphire betas per chunk, with a max size of 6 ores per beta. It has a 60% chance of not being generated when facing air.\n\n..."
